    replaces the DOS resource with the same value (id). path is the PNG file, relative to the folder.
    x and y are the image's origin (anchor) in Mac pixels; SDLPoP places Mac images by it.
    A DAT file listed here is a Mac set: an image it lacks is drawn blank, so the gap shows.
    Only the font and the DOS credits (title.dat 45) fall back to the DOS images.
-->

